{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1220257-sorcerer-20","id":1220257,"title":"Sorcerer 20?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-19T08:43:29-07:00","id":1220257,"title":"Sorcerer 20?","content":"Just wondering if anyone knows if there are plans to revise Sorcerer? I guess, I don't feel it needs revision (except for more on Extraordinary Citizens &lt;_&lt;), but I've been wondering if it's something on the docket.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Hosting <a href=\"http://opx-finalfrontier.wikidot.com\" target=\"_blank\">Outpost Phoenix</a>, an Non-Affiliated, Live-Action Star Trek <a href=\"https://discord.gg/6zwnyzm\" target=\"_blank\">Discord</a> Sim. New players are always welcome!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11235-arzie","name":"Arzie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11235_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T08:51:32-07:00","id":1220259,"title":"","content":"is Sorcer still canon? is a valid question<br /> <br /> a lot of its numina are WAY more powerful then you see in hunters hunted or kinfolk a breed apart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T09:36:46-07:00","id":1220265,"title":"","content":"It's weird, but despite Mage being the umbrella for mortal magic (Sorcerer Revised was basically a Mage book, by the time it was published), it seems like every other splat in the 20th Anniversary line seems more interested in tackling Sorcery. Hunters Hunted II, Kinfolk: A Breed Apart, DAV20: Tome of Secrets.<br /> <br /> Then again, those other lines have produced far more books, far more quickly.<br /> <br /> What's also weird is that those other books seem to have more to say about about pre-Sphere magick. DAV20 Tome of Secrets touched a bit on it, and Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra included a full set of Foundaiton and Pillars for Itarajani mages.<br /> <br /> <br /> So is Onyx Path/White Wolf ever going to make a proper Sorcerer 20th? I doubt it. Some of it might be redundant, given those other books already released. Maybe when the 5th Edition books start coming out, we might get a proper book that collects all Sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T09:40:01-07:00","id":1220267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1220257-sorcerer-20?p=1220259#post1220259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is Sorcer still canon? is a valid question</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not so much that it's not canon - the 20th anniversary edition of books are generally, by default, metaplot agnostic. M20 mostly skirted around the matter of Sorcerer for the sake of brevity. M20 was a huge book. So huge they've had to break off chunks of material intended for the core book, in order to put it in other books.<br /> <br /> It can be forgiven, then, for not wanting to tackle an entire other magic and character creation system JUST for mortals, when the Sphere system and its surrounding Focus stuff already takes so much pagecount.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T11:41:30-07:00","id":1220290,"title":"","content":"I guess my biggest reason for wondering this is that there are a few MUSHs and other online games that still have Mortal+ spheres. There's one, especially, where the only option to play a Technocratic-leaning person is to play an Extraordinary Citizen. I've had the PDF for Revised for ever, and I've been looking at getting the hardcopy, but if a 20-Version is going to come out anytime soon, I'd like to know before I buy it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Hosting <a href=\"http://opx-finalfrontier.wikidot.com\" target=\"_blank\">Outpost Phoenix</a>, an Non-Affiliated, Live-Action Star Trek <a href=\"https://discord.gg/6zwnyzm\" target=\"_blank\">Discord</a> Sim. New players are always welcome!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11235-arzie","name":"Arzie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11235_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T11:59:30-07:00","id":1220296,"title":"","content":"In a setting where Mages are fully covered, Sorcerers will always need to have changes made to them. In VtM, Mages aren't center stage, so representing magical mortals as sorcerers is a neat way of dealing with the issue.<br /> <br /> With Mages having a fully developed set of Sects and a complex history and Sphere system, I feel like Sorcerers in Mage are best used as NPCs, simply being Unawakened occultists. They simply learn Rotes rather than Spheres, and use Attribute + Ability for dice pools. This makes them Specialists rather than Generalists.<br /> <br /> Difficulty is determined by the highest level Sphere in the rote being used +4. For example, a Sorcerer who had learnt to create and launch a blast of golden flames would roll their Wits + Occult at difficulty 7, inflicting damage the way a Mage would with a Prime 3 + Forces 2 effect. The key difference being that the Mage in question might be able to inflict a load of Lethal or Aggravated damage with their hedge magic, but they can't use a node or manipulate electricity or hear radiowaves without taking Rotes which reflect those capabilities.<br /> <br /> Technically speaking a Sorcerer who knew enough Rotes and had very high Attributes and Abilities might end up being much more powerful than a Mage PC will ever become, but this would cost much more EXP than simply developing the necessary Sphere levels to cover the effects of all of these Rotes and much more. The &quot;High Priest&quot; pawn of a Nephandus might be able to call upon the Unholy Host, inflict a death curse and make himself immune to fire, along with 70 or so other powerful infernal rotes, but unless he knows a Rote for forcing a Cyborg to reject its mechanical components (he likely doesn't) he might be killed in a single round by a Mark V.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T14:48:38-07:00","id":1220344,"title":"","content":"Unless I missed something, it's possible we might be getting some of this in the upcoming Gods, Monsters, and Familiar Strangers book from the M20 stretch goals, since it seems a reasonable place to cover what's in Sorcerer Revised. IIRC, the projected size of GM&amp;FS is big enough to fit all of Sorcerer Revised and the Familiar section from Forged by Dragon's Fire in it combined, though that wouldn't leave much in for more things to cover. So if we're going to see Sorcery in that book, it would have to be condensed (perhaps not separating Sorcery and Psychic powers and having them use the same base powers with different rules to differentiate them).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T18:53:35-07:00","id":1222335,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure that Gods, Monsters, and Familiar Strangers is about non-human and artificial human characters; I will be surprised if it includes anything about sorcery.<br /> <br /> I also don't expect Mr. Brucato to tackle Sorcery any time soon; as you say, the existing books work reasonably well, and as others say he's got plenty else on his plate. And I wouldn't want S20 as a M20 supplement anyway; I'd much prefer it as a standalone World of Darkness supplement the way the first edition was \u2014 more on my thoughts on the matter are <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/559836-updating-and-expanding-sorcerer\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> That said, one fairly simple change that could be leveraged to great effect would be to replace Sorcerer's Foci with M20's Practices: that is, every Sorcerer has a Practice; and that Practice determines not only what Instruments he uses but also which Abilities are used to form the dice pools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T10:05:08-07:00","id":1224738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1220257-sorcerer-20?p=1220296#post1220296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I feel like Sorcerers in Mage are best used as NPCs, simply being Unawakened occultists. They simply learn Rotes rather than Spheres, and use Attribute + Ability for dice pools. This makes them Specialists rather than Generalists.<br /> <br /> Difficulty is determined by the highest level Sphere in the rote being used +4. For example, a Sorcerer who had learnt to create and launch a blast of golden flames would roll their Wits + Occult at difficulty 7, inflicting damage the way a Mage would with a Prime 3 + Forces 2 effect. The key difference being that the Mage in question might be able to inflict a load of Lethal or Aggravated damage with their hedge magic, but they can't use a node or manipulate electricity or hear radiowaves without taking Rotes which reflect those capabilities.<br /> <br /> Technically speaking a Sorcerer who knew enough Rotes and had very high Attributes and Abilities might end up being much more powerful than a Mage PC will ever become, but this would cost much more EXP than simply developing the necessary Sphere levels to cover the effects of all of these Rotes and much more. The &quot;High Priest&quot; pawn of a Nephandus might be able to call upon the Unholy Host, inflict a death curse and make himself immune to fire, along with 70 or so other powerful infernal rotes, but unless he knows a Rote for forcing a Cyborg to reject its mechanical components (he likely doesn't) he might be killed in a single round by a Mark V.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree with this idea of Sorcerers being able to learn and cast the same Rotes that Mages can learn and cast. I think that it is good and very characterful, that Sorcerers simply can do - if words can at all describe the disparity in variety, potential, and power - much, much less than Mages.<br /> <br /> I think that the very limited scope of Sorcery Paths compared to spellcasting capabilities of Mages is justified and evocative.<br /> For example, Sorcerers practically can't do anything similar to Forces Spells and Rotes ; only direct attacks with conjured elements and maybe influencing the weather. This is because a Sorcerer, unlike a Mage, just does not understand for example that : there is more to spellcasting than functionality - while at the same time the spellcasting itself and how it is done is where the truth might be looked for and found. Mages instinctually and/or intellectually feel and understand this, and/or other concepts. Also, Mages have much more comprehensive and deep Paradigms than Sorcerers. Thus Sorcerers don't get anything close to Forces Effects of Mages in variety, potential and power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 06-04-2018, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}